@page "/docs/utilities/shimmer"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Shimmer
<PageTitle>Shimmer - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Shimmer</h1>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">Utilities</BzBadge>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">CSS only</BzBadge>
        </div>
        <p>A highlight that sweeps across text or a surface to show that something is still being written or a step is still running. <code>shimmer</code> clips the band to the glyphs of a line of text, while <code>shimmer-block</code> sweeps a surface such as a placeholder tile, and <a class="text-foreground font-medium" href="docs/components/skeleton">Skeleton</a> is built on that surface mode. The band is derived from the element's own color, so it works on any text color in light and dark mode with nothing to configure, and the text underneath stays at full strength for contrast checks.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(ShimmerUsageExample)"
                Setup="@null"
                Description="Add one class to the text. There is nothing to install or register, because the utilities ship in the stylesheet Blaizio already imports into your Tailwind entry point." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default"
          Description="The same class on four different colors and sizes. Size the element to its text, here with `w-fit`, so the band sweeps across the glyphs rather than an empty box."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Surface mode"
          Description="`shimmer-block` sweeps the element's own fill rather than its text, which is what a skeleton or placeholder tile needs. Every option below works on it too."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerBlockExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Color"
          Description="`shimmer-color-*` sets the band's color while the text keeps its own. Any theme color works, and a bracketed value takes anything CSS accepts."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerColorExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Speed, spread and angle"
          Description="Duration is in milliseconds, spread is the band's width as a percentage of the sweep, and angle is in degrees. An angle of 90 runs straight along the line, and lower values tilt it."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerTuningExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Playback"
          Description="Run a single pass instead of a loop, reverse the sweep, or turn the effect off to restore plain text."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerPlaybackExample)" />

    <Demo Title="In context"
          Description="The effect on the title of a running step, and on a card heading whose body is still loading as skeletons."
          Example="typeof(ShimmerInContextExample)" />

    <section class="space-y-6">
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Class reference</h2>
        <ClassTable Rows="@Classes" />
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Notes</h2>
        <p>The effect paints the text with a gradient (<code>background-clip: text</code>) and empties the glyphs with <code>-webkit-text-fill-color</code> rather than <code>color</code>, so the gradient can still read the element's own color, which is what lets the band be derived from it. The glyphs themselves are filled by a solid <code>background-color: currentColor</code> underneath, which is what keeps the resting text at full contrast.</p>
        <p>The sweep follows the reading direction, so it runs right to left in a right-to-left subtree automatically. Reduced motion switches it off and leaves plain text, because unlike the scroll fade, this effect moves on its own.</p>
        <p>It is decoration, not information. Keep the sentence itself honest ("Generating response...") so a reader who never sees the animation still knows what is happening.</p>
    </section>
</div>

@code {
    private static readonly (string, string[], string)[] Classes =
    [
        ("shimmer",
        [
            "background-color: currentColor;",
            "background-image: linear-gradient(var(--bz-shimmer-angle, 100deg), transparent calc(50% - var(--bz-shimmer-spread, 12%)), var(--bz-shimmer-highlight, color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 45%, var(--color-background))) 50%, transparent calc(50% + var(--bz-shimmer-spread, 12%)));",
            "background-size: 200% 100%;",
            "background-clip: text;",
            "-webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;",
            "animation: bz-shimmer-sweep var(--bz-shimmer-duration, 2s) linear;",
            "animation-iteration-count: var(--bz-shimmer-iterations, infinite);",
            "animation-direction: var(--bz-shimmer-direction, normal);",
        ],
        "Text mode: the glyphs stay at full strength and the band, clipped to them, is a sheen mixed towards the page behind."),

        ("shimmer-block",
        [
            "background-image: linear-gradient(var(--bz-shimmer-angle, 100deg), transparent calc(50% - var(--bz-shimmer-spread, 12%)), var(--bz-shimmer-highlight, color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 15%, transparent)) 50%, transparent calc(50% + var(--bz-shimmer-spread, 12%)));",
            "background-size: 200% 100%;",
            "animation: bz-shimmer-sweep var(--bz-shimmer-duration, 2s) linear;",
            "animation-iteration-count: var(--bz-shimmer-iterations, infinite);",
            "animation-direction: var(--bz-shimmer-direction, normal);",
        ],
        "Surface mode: the band paints over the element's own fill. What Skeleton uses."),

        ("shimmer-color-<color>",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-highlight: <color>;",
        ],
        "The highlight color: a theme color (shimmer-color-primary) or a bracketed value."),

        ("shimmer-duration-<number>",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-duration: calc(<number> * 1ms);",
        ],
        "One sweep's length in milliseconds. Defaults to 2000."),

        ("shimmer-spread-<number>",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-spread: calc(<number> * 1%);",
        ],
        "The band's width as a percentage of the sweep. Defaults to 12."),

        ("shimmer-angle-<number>",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-angle: calc(<number> * 1deg);",
        ],
        "The band's tilt in degrees. Defaults to 100."),

        ("shimmer-once",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-iterations: 1;",
        ],
        "Plays a single pass instead of looping."),

        ("shimmer-reverse",
        [
            "--bz-shimmer-direction: reverse;",
            "--bz-shimmer-direction-rtl: normal;",
        ],
        "Sweeps the other way. The RTL pairing keeps one flip from canceling the other."),

        ("shimmer-none",
        [
            "background-image: none;",
            "animation-name: none;",
            "-webkit-text-fill-color: currentColor;",
        ],
        "No sweep. Replaces shimmer or shimmer-block when both are present."),
    ];
}
